From: PaperMono Zephyr contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dma: esp32: scope memory-to-memory case declarations

Zephyr 4.4.1's ESP32 GDMA driver declares local variables directly after a
case label.  The Xtensa GCC toolchain rejects that construct when the project
is compiled with the C17 language mode selected by this workspace.  Give the
case its own compound scope without changing runtime behavior.

diff --git a/drivers/dma/dma_esp32_gdma.c b/drivers/dma/dma_esp32_gdma.c
index 1b1427d8..eaff3bae 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/dma_esp32_gdma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/dma_esp32_gdma.c
@@ -376,7 +376,7 @@ static int dma_esp32_config(const struct device *dev, uint32_t channel,
 	dma_channel->channel_id = channel / 2;
 
 	switch (config_dma->channel_direction) {
-	case MEMORY_TO_MEMORY:
+	case MEMORY_TO_MEMORY: {
 		/*
 		 *	Create both Tx and Rx stream on the same channel_id
 		 */
@@ -394,6 +394,7 @@ static int dma_esp32_config(const struct device *dev, uint32_t channel,
 		ret = dma_esp32_config_rx(dev, dma_channel_rx, config_dma);
 		ret = dma_esp32_config_tx(dev, dma_channel_tx, config_dma);
 		break;
+	}
 	case PERIPHERAL_TO_MEMORY:
 		ret = dma_esp32_config_rx(dev, dma_channel, config_dma);
 		break;
-- 
2.51.0
